    "<div style=\"left:0px;top:0px;height:14px;line-height:14px;\">",
    "A dock can be given a drag modifier, which is off unless asked for. While it is held, dragging anywhere in a window, its bar and tabs included, moves </div>",
    "</div>",
    "<div style=\"left:0px;top:14px;width:779.03125px;height:14px;font:normal 300 12px Ubuntu, system-ui, -apple-system, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;color:rgba(141,153,174,1);\">",
    "<div style=\"left:0.40625px;top:0px;height:14px;line-height:14px;\">",
    "the whole window, and dragging with the right button resizes it from its nearest edge or corner, or moves the split nearest the pointer in a docked </div>",
    "</div>",
    "<div style=\"left:0px;top:28px;width:458.95313px;height:14px;font:normal 300 12px Ubuntu, system-ui, -apple-system, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;color:rgba(141,153,174,1);\">",
    "<div style=\"left:0.03125px;top:0px;height:14px;line-height:14px;\">",
    "pane. Nothing in the dock or its tabs sees those presses. The Linux desktop uses Super.</div>",
    "</div>",
